{"game": "space-marine-2011", "language": "english", "appid": 55150, "month": "2026-05", "window": 4, "start_date": 1779580800, "end_date": 1780271999, "month_true_total": 81, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-10-09 18:08:29 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "226906214", "author": {"steamid": "76561198040235958", "personaname": "ParrotMan01", "persona_status": "in-game", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/ParrotMan01/", "num_games_owned": 638, "num_reviews": 158, "playtime_forever": 525, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 525, "last_played": 1780269451, "avatar": "049116dc3827584518d1124b90aa06b7fab8d023"}, "language": "english", "review": "I had almost forgotten how this game came out during the 7th gen consoles. The final boss is a QTE, which is probably my biggest complaint with this game. Outside of that, the game made me feel powerful and fragile.  I would die extremely quickly or I would be ripping and tearing before DOOM 2016 popularized it more.\r\nIt's good.  I'm glad I played it on PC.  The enemy counts are absurd and I got high frame rates that held steady.  I encountered a consistent crash that required me to verify the game's files.  There's bugs where NPCs required to progress the story simply don't move.  One time I had to walk behind an NPC and push her into the elevator to get the cutscene to start.  Enemies would get stuck on walls.  Basically funny and annoying bugs that didn't ruin the experience. I bring this up because this may happen to you too.\r\n\r\nOne last thing, I know next to nothing about Warhammer. I would have been too poor to fully participate in that hobby.  That's why I'm glad more Warhammer games are coming. I get to experience at least parts of this universe.  I'd consider this game a classic, so I do recommend it.", "timestamp_created": 1780269738, "timestamp_updated": 1780269738, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 2, "votes_funny": 1, "weighted_vote_score": "0.537572264671325684", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1315281600", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "226897590", "author": {"steamid": "76561198843872025", "personaname": "popnoob", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198843872025/", "num_games_owned": 53, "num_reviews": 12, "playtime_forever": 789, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 789, "last_played": 1780260572, "avatar": "1df3535a6f4c9bcf76d310fff46700d18b98412c"}, "language": "english", "review": "very good game", "timestamp_created": 1780260619, "timestamp_updated": 1780260619, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.519999980926513672", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": true, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1315281600", "hardware": {"system_ram": "16215", "os": "Windows 11", "cpu_name": "Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-10300H CPU @ 2.50GHz", "adapter_description": "NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1650", "vram_size": 3950}, "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "226835934", "author": {"steamid": "76561198355395456", "personaname": "C.E.O MINDSET", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198355395456/", "num_games_owned": 423, "num_reviews": 21, "playtime_forever": 1469, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1469, "last_played": 1780202035, "avatar": "cc9f81c1e4424e97d2a5448ee2c94aa088741af2"}, "language": "english", "review": "The best warhammer 40k game in existence, ironically better than space marine 2 with far more content...oh by the way here is a link for the fix bugsplat error (https://github.com/adrian-lebioda/SpaceMarineCoreFix/releases) put in your game files directory the [8.dll] file and it will work just fine...also why the ♥♥♥♥